"""TPSM336xx-Q1 — TI 36 V automotive synchronous buck power modules (HotRod QFN-FCMOD-11).

Family reference design covering the TPSM33606-Q1 (0.6 A), TPSM33610-Q1
(1 A) and TPSM33620-Q1 (2 A) orderables — same pinout, package and
datasheet. Selection is by `output_current` and `output_voltage`:

    output_voltage  silicon  MPN family per i_max
    --------------  -------  ----------------------------------------
    3.3 V (fixed)   S3 trim  TPSM33606S3 / 33610S3 / 33620S3 QRDNRQ1
    5   V (fixed)   S5 trim  TPSM33606S5 / 33610S5 / 33620S5 QRDNRQ1
    other 1.2–5 V   S3 + FB  S3 silicon, FB divider sets V_OUT

For 3.3 V or 5 V exactly, the matching factory-trim silicon is used
with FB jumpered to VOUT. For any other voltage in 1.2 V – 5 V the IC
runs adjustable per §7.3.2.1 (FB-resistance startup detect overrides
the trim).

The smallest sufficient current tier becomes the primary `part`;
larger tiers are BOM alternatives (drop-in with extra headroom).

Not included: `TPSM336203QRDNRQ1` (2 A / 3.3 V alt orderable, no
DRSS — instantiate explicitly if EMI behaviour warrants).

Circuit (datasheet §8.2 / Tables 8-2, 8-3)
- C_IN1 (4.7 µF, 0805, 50 V X7R) + C_IN2 (100 nF, 0402, 50 V X7R)
  input bypass per §8.2.2.3 / Table 8-5. 50 V matches TI's reference.
- C_OUT1 / C_OUT2 (2 × 22 µF, 0805, 10 V X7R) output bulk per Table
  8-2. After DC-bias derating: ~30 µF effective at 3.3 V (~70 %
  retention at 33 % bias), ~22 µF at 5 V (~50 % at 50 % bias) —
  sufficient for sub-mV ripple at 2.2 MHz and steady-load regulation.
  **Additional bulk may be required at the usage site** (up to ~10 ×
  the design value or 1000 µF per §8.2.2.4) depending on:
    - V_IN / V_OUT ratio (lower duty cycle → higher inductor ripple)
    - load current and step magnitude / di/dt (§8.2.2.4 sets a
      40 µF effective minimum for fast transients on the 2 A part)
    - downstream LDO / PSRR-sensitive loads
    - long input cable runs / large input impedance
- C_VCC (1 µF, 0402, 10 V X7R) bypasses the internal 3.3 V LDO.
- BOOT (pin 7) NotConnected — 100 nF C_BOOT integrated (§7.3.7).
- SW (pins 5, 6) NotConnected — datasheet pin table forbids external
  loading; copper must be minimised for EMI.
- FB divider (§7.3.2):
  - Fixed (3.3 V / 5 V): R_FBT = 0 Ω jumper, R_FBB DNP, C_FF DNP.
  - Adjustable (1.2–5 V): R_FBT = 10 kΩ × V_OUT, R_FBB = 10 kΩ ×
    V_OUT / (V_OUT − V_FB), V_FB = 1 V — keeps R_par ≈ 10 kΩ per
    Eq 3 / Table 7-1. C_FF = 10 pF (§7.3.6).
- R_EN: 100 kΩ to VIN; on by default. DNP via `pullup_en=False` when
  EN is driven externally. Per §7.3.3 EN must not float.
- MODE/SYNC strap via `mode` config (§7.3.4); pulls to VCC (within
  the 5.5 V abs-max). Per §7.3.4 must not float.
  - AUTO (default): R_MODE_PD populated, R_MODE_PU DNP — PFM at light load
  - FPWM: R_MODE_PU populated, R_MODE_PD DNP — forced PWM
  - EXTERNAL: both DNP — caller drives the pin (e.g. 2.2 MHz sync clock)
- PGOOD: open-drain; add external pull-up if consumed.
"""

load("@stdlib/checks.zen", "voltage_within")
load("@stdlib/units.zen", "Current", "Resistance", "Voltage")
load("@stdlib/utils.zen", "e96")

Capacitor = Module("@stdlib/generics/Capacitor.zen")
Resistor = Module("@stdlib/generics/Resistor.zen")

_V_FB = Voltage("1V")  # Internal reference (datasheet §6, V_FB)
_R_PAR = Resistance("10kohm")  # Target R_FBT ‖ R_FBB (datasheet §7.3.2.1)


# Adjustable-mode feedback divider (datasheet §7.3.2.1):
#   R_FBT × R_FBB / (R_FBT + R_FBB) = R_par   (parallel held at ~10 kΩ)
#   V_OUT = V_FB × (1 + R_FBT / R_FBB)
def _r_fbt(v_out):
    return e96(_R_PAR * v_out / _V_FB)


def _r_fbb(v_out):
    return e96(_R_PAR * v_out / (v_out - _V_FB))


ModeSync = enum("AUTO", "FPWM", "EXTERNAL")

# (mpn, symbol, i_max, v_trim) - ordered ascending by i_max so the smallest
# sufficient tier becomes the primary part. All six orderables share the
# same RDN package, pinout, datasheet, and AEC-Q100 grade with DRSS.
_FAMILY = [
    ("TPSM33606S3QRDNRQ1", "TPSM33606S3", Current("0.6A"), Voltage("3.3V")),
    ("TPSM33606S5QRDNRQ1", "TPSM33606S5", Current("0.6A"), Voltage("5V")),
    ("TPSM33610S3QRDNRQ1", "TPSM33610S3", Current("1A"), Voltage("3.3V")),
    ("TPSM33610S5QRDNRQ1", "TPSM33610S5", Current("1A"), Voltage("5V")),
    ("TPSM33620S3QRDNRQ1", "TPSM33620S3", Current("2A"), Voltage("3.3V")),
    ("TPSM33620S5QRDNRQ1", "TPSM33620S5", Current("2A"), Voltage("5V")),
]


def _check_current(i):
    check(
        i <= Current("2A"),
        "output_current must be ≤ 2 A (family max), got " + str(i),
    )


output_voltage = config(
    Voltage,
    default="3.3V",
    checks=voltage_within("1.2V to 5V"),
)
output_current = config(Current, default="2A", checks=_check_current, help="Minimum required I_OUT.")
pullup_en = config(bool, default=True, help="Populate 100 kΩ EN→VIN pull-up (always-on default).")
mode = config(
    ModeSync,
    default=ModeSync("AUTO"),
    help="MODE/SYNC strap: AUTO=PFM at light load, FPWM=forced PWM, EXTERNAL=both DNP (caller drives pin).",
)

# Pick the silicon whose factory trim is closer to the target VOUT.
# 3.3 V / 5 V → exact match, IC runs in fixed-trim mode (FB jumpered).
# Other allowed voltages → adjustable mode on the closer trim; the IC
# senses the FB divider resistance at startup and overrides the trim
# (datasheet §7.3.2.1). Either trim works, but matching the closer
# value minimises startup transient before divider detection.
_v_trim = Voltage("5V") if output_voltage >= Voltage("4V") else Voltage("3.3V")
_is_fixed = output_voltage == _v_trim

# Smallest sufficient current tier is primary; larger tiers are alternates.
_matches = [(mpn, sym) for mpn, sym, i_max, v in _FAMILY if i_max >= output_current and v == _v_trim]
_parts = [Part(mpn=mpn, manufacturer="Texas Instruments", qualifications=["AEC-Q100"]) for mpn, _ in _matches]

VIN = io(Power(voltage="3V to 36V"))
VOUT = io(Power(voltage=output_voltage))
GND = io(Ground())
EN = io(Net(), optional=True, help="Enable; pulled to VIN by default (see `pullup_en`).")
PGOOD = io(Net(), optional=True, help="Open-drain power-good; needs external pull-up.")
MODE_SYNC = io(Net(), optional=True, help="MODE/SYNC; strap behavior set by `mode`.")

_VCC = Power("VCC")
_FB = Net("FB")

Component(
    name="U1",
    symbol=Symbol(library="TPSM336xx-Q1.kicad_sym", name=_matches[0][1]),
    part=_parts[0],
    properties={"alternatives": _parts[1:]},
    pins={
        "VIN": VIN,
        "VOUT": VOUT,
        "GND": GND,
        "EN": EN,
        "FB": _FB,
        "PGOOD": PGOOD,
        "MODE/SYNC": MODE_SYNC,
        "VCC": _VCC,
        "BOOT": NotConnected(),  # Internal 100 nF C_BOOT (datasheet §7.3.7)
        "SW": NotConnected(),  # Datasheet pin table: do not connect externally
    },
)

# Input decoupling (datasheet §8.2.2.3 / Table 8-5).
Capacitor(name="C_IN1", value="4.7uF", voltage="50V", package="0805", P1=VIN, P2=GND)
Capacitor(name="C_IN2", value="100nF", voltage="50V", package="0402", P1=VIN, P2=GND)

# Output decoupling - 2 × 22 μF per Table 8-2 (covers all current
# tiers in the family). Integrators add bulk for fast-transient
# performance per §8.2.2.4.
Capacitor(name="C_OUT1", value="22uF", voltage="10V", package="0805", P1=VOUT, P2=GND)
Capacitor(name="C_OUT2", value="22uF", voltage="10V", package="0805", P1=VOUT, P2=GND)

# VCC bypass on the internal LDO (datasheet §8.2.2)
Capacitor(name="C_VCC", value="1uF", voltage="10V", package="0402", P1=_VCC, P2=GND)

# Feedback (datasheet §7.3.2):
#   Fixed:       R_FBT = 0 Ω jumper, R_FBB / C_FF DNP - silicon trim sets V_OUT.
#   Adjustable:  R_FBT/R_FBB sized via _r_fbt/_r_fbb above; C_FF = 10 pF.
if _is_fixed:
    _r_fbt_value = Resistance("0ohm")
    _r_fbb_value = Resistance("10kohm")
else:
    _r_fbt_value = _r_fbt(output_voltage).with_tolerance("1%")
    _r_fbb_value = _r_fbb(output_voltage).with_tolerance("1%")

Resistor(name="R_FBT", value=_r_fbt_value, package="0402", P1=VOUT, P2=_FB)
Resistor(name="R_FBB", value=_r_fbb_value, package="0402", dnp=_is_fixed, P1=_FB, P2=GND)
Capacitor(name="C_FF", value="10pF", voltage="50V", package="0402", dnp=_is_fixed, P1=VOUT, P2=_FB)

# EN pull-up to VIN keeps the module enabled by default (datasheet §7.3.3).
Resistor(name="R_EN", value="100kohm", package="0402", dnp=not pullup_en, P1=VIN, P2=EN)

# MODE/SYNC strap (datasheet §7.3.4) - exactly one of these is populated
# in AUTO/FPWM, both DNP for EXTERNAL drive.
Resistor(
    name="R_MODE_PU",
    value="100kohm",
    package="0402",
    dnp=mode != ModeSync("FPWM"),
    P1=_VCC,
    P2=MODE_SYNC,
)
Resistor(
    name="R_MODE_PD",
    value="100kohm",
    package="0402",
    dnp=mode != ModeSync("AUTO"),
    P1=MODE_SYNC,
    P2=GND,
)

Layout("TPSM336xx-Q1", path="layout/TPSM336xx-Q1")

# pcb:sch C_FF.C x=-148.3200 y=-115.3000 rot=0
# pcb:sch C_IN1.C x=-783.3200 y=-115.3000 rot=0
